# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the C client.
#
# The .NET runtime gives each thread that uses its wait subsystem a native mutex and
# condition variable (88 bytes). They are owned by managed objects on the garbage
# collected heap, which LeakSanitizer does not scan, and are released when the thread
# ends, after the process exit at which the leak check runs. So they show up as
# "direct leaks" although nothing is lost.
#
# Suppress exactly that allocation site. Anything the library hands to the client,
# such as a result not passed to vault_sealed_free, is allocated elsewhere
# (Vault.Native's ToNative) and is still reported.
leak:SystemNative_LowLevelMonitor_Create
